  "description_title": "Luxury Serviced Apartments in Singapore",
  "description": "<p>Ascott Raffles Place Singapore offers an exceptional stay in the vibrant heart of Singapore’s Central Business District (CBD). This distinguished serviced residence is housed within a beautifully restored 1950s heritage structure, showcasing an elegant Art Deco façade that creates a striking contrast against the city’s contemporary skyline. Guests seeking a refined apartment in Singapore will find themselves perfectly positioned for both crucial business engagements and leisurely exploration, with immediate access to a dynamic array of cultural, entertainment, and sophisticated shopping destinations within the CBD and Marina Bay precinct.</p>\n<p>Each spacious apartment offers a welcoming, refined sanctuary, featuring modern furnishings and thoughtful amenities for absolute comfort and convenience. Whether you choose a sophisticated studio or an expansive multi-bedroom suite, every detail ensures an elevated residential living experience. Guests benefit from complimentary high-speed wireless internet connectivity, a fully equipped designer kitchen for personalised meal preparation, and a premium BOSE home entertainment system for relaxation. This makes Ascott Raffles Place Singapore an ideal choice for discerning global travellers seeking sophisticated long-stay apartments in Singapore.</p>\n<p>The property offers a comprehensive selection of facilities and signature services to enhance your stay. Guests can take a refreshing dip in the stunning infinity swimming pool overlooking the skyline, maintain their fitness routine in the well-appointed gymnasium, or find a quiet moment in The Living Room, our exclusive residents' lounge. For dining, CALI, our on-site restaurant, offers an exceptional all-day menu of Western cuisine, featuring dishes such as succulent braised beef cheeks and gourmet wagyu burgers. Engage with the Ascott Lifestyle through our curated residents' programmes, which focus on culture, gastronomy, and wellness, offering unique opportunities to connect with the city's rich tapestry.</p>\n<p>Beyond the private comforts of your apartment, Ascott Raffles Place Singapore provides an array of bespoke services to cater to your every need. Benefit from 24/7 on-call wellness and security, ensuring peace of mind throughout your stay. Our dedicated team provides daily housekeeping services (excluding Sundays and public holidays), alongside convenient laundry and dry cleaning options. We are committed to ensuring comfort for all guests, offering accessible rooms and facilities for those with physical requirements. For those planning an extended visit, we provide a seamless blend of attentive service and residential comfort, ensuring every stay feels like an exceptional home.<br /><br /><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Going Cashless</strong><br /></span>In order to enhance your guest experience, please note that the property will only be accepting the following payment methods: Credit card, debit card, secured online payment, mobile payment and electronic bank transfer.<br /><br /></p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong>Identity Verification Requirement</strong></span></p>\n<p>In accordance with the National Registration Regulations (Regulation 17), we kindly request that all guests present a valid physical ID or passport for identity verification upon entry.</p>\n<p>Please note that other forms of identification, including work permit cards, foreign worker In-principle approval (IPA), driving licenses, and membership cards, will not be accepted.</p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><strong><br />Ascott Clean360</strong></span><br />Ascott Raffles Place Singapore has implemented the Ascott Clean360 commitment to safety, wellness and cleanliness. More info <span style=\"color: #0000ff;\"><strong><a style=\"color: #0000ff;\" href=\"https://www.discoverasr.com/en/ascott-cares/respect/ascott-clean360\">here</a></strong></span>.<br /><br /><strong><u>Sustainability Information<br /></u></strong>Carbon Footprint: <span lang=\"EN-GB\">36.66 kg per room nigh</span>t - performing above peer average in Singapore. <br />Water Footprint: <span lang=\"EN-GB\">319.54 litres per room night - amongst top 25% peers in Singapore. </span></p>",
